# The network link to beehive is dependable (plan phase H3): it is saved and
# comes back after a restart, it reconnects when beehive was away, and a
# wish filed meanwhile is delivered afterwards.
@net
@ai-net
@disk
$ net dhcp
~ 10\.0\.2\.15
$ ai connect {hive} {hive-name} {hive-key}
~ ^connecting to beehive as machine 'test' \(saved\)$
connected (fake fake)
$ cat /system/hive
~ ^name test$

# beehive goes away: the OS notices, and says so instead of waiting.
@hive stop
$ ping -c 2 10.0.2.2
$ ai
~ ^bridge:      network, as machine 'test': not connected: beehive
$ ask anyone there
~ offline|not connected|not running
$ wish remembered while beehive was away
Thanks! Saved to /system/inbox/signals.jsonl.

# It comes back: the OS connects again by itself and delivers the wish.
@hive start
$ ping -c 6 10.0.2.2
$ ai
~ beehive online \(fake fake\)
$ ask are you back
Question: are you back

# After a restart of the OS the link is there again, without typing anything.
@reboot
$ net dhcp
$ ping -c 4 10.0.2.2
$ ai
~ ^bridge:      network, as machine 'test': beehive online \(fake fake\)
$ ask after the restart
Question: after the restart
$ log 60
~ "event":"hive"|hive
!~ 10\.0\.2\.2
@signal "target": "test", "kind": "wish", "text": "remembered while beehive was away"
